##
## Description  
##   Derivatives of curves
## EndDescription

## Tagged by ynw2d

## DBsubject(Calculus - multivariable)
## DBchapter(Calculus of vector valued functions)
## DBsection(Derivatives)
## Institution(Dartmouth)
## Author(Stewart)
## MLT(der_tangent_line)
## Level(3)
## TitleText1('Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Stewart')
## EditionText1('5')
## Section1('14.2')
## Problem1('')
## TitleText2('Calculus: Early Transcendentals')
## AuthorText2('Rogawski')
## EditionText2('1')
## Section2('13.2')
## Problem2('36')
## KEYWORDS('derivative' 'parametric' 'vector')

## local/Library/272/setStewart13_2/problem_9.pg

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
  "PGstandard.pl",
  "PGchoicemacros.pl",
  "PGgraphmacros.pl",
  "Dartmouthmacros.pl",
  "PGcourse.pl"
);
 

## Do NOT show partial correct answers
$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

$a = random(2,5);
$b = random(2,5);
$c = random(1,5);
$t0 = random(1,3);


$x0 = $t0**($a) - 1;
$y0 = $t0**($b) + 1;
$z0 = $t0**($c);
## Ok, we are ready to begin the problem...
##
TEXT(beginproblem());


BEGIN_TEXT
$BR

Soit le chemin
\[ \mathbf{r}(t) = \left(t^{$a} - 1\right)\mathbf{i} + \left(t^{$b} + 1\right)\mathbf{j} + t^{$c}\,\mathbf{k}.
\]
Trouver l'approximation linéaire \(\mathbf{L}(t) = \mathbf{r}(t_0) + (t-t_0)\,\mathbf{r}'(t_0)\) de \(\mathbf{r}\) au point \(($x0, $y0, $z0)\), c'est-à-dire en \(t_0 = $t0\). Son image est la droite tangente à la courbe en ce point.
Entrer les composantes de \(\mathbf{L}(t)\) en fonction de \(t\).

 $BR


\( L_1(t) = \)\{ans_rule(25)\},$BR
\( L_2(t) = \)\{ans_rule(25 )\},$BR
\( L_3(t) = \)\{ans_rule(25)\}
$PAR
END_TEXT

 ANS(fun_cmp("$x0 + (t - $t0)*$a*$t0**($a - 1)", vars=>["t"]));
 ANS(fun_cmp("$y0 + (t - $t0)*$b*$t0**($b-1)", vars=>["t"]));
 ANS(fun_cmp("$z0 + (t - $t0)*$c*$t0**($c-1)", vars=>["t"]));
ENDDOCUMENT();




